---
/**
 * woodworks / PageBW — "Molave" (custom cabinetry + furniture, one workshop).
 *
 * Workshop grey and safety orange: Archivo on its WIDTH axis (72-85% for the
 * condensed display cuts, 115% for the wide wordmark) over Archivo body copy,
 * with JetBrains Mono for every small label — eyebrows, part numbers, the
 * address ledger, the footer index. Ink hairlines everywhere, no radii, no
 * shadows except the floating pill's hard offset. Three full-width black
 * bands (the marquee, the process band, the footer) and one orange one (the
 * closing band).
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet, skip link, anchor pass, map boot). It does NOT
 * compose with BaseLayout, and it is the only file in the variant that reads
 * `siteData`; the sixteen section components receive `layout` + `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. It only READS layout.businessName /
 * layout.tagline (<title>), content.description (<meta name="description">),
 * layout.favicon and layout.ogImage. Every data-field / data-image-field /
 * data-href-field lives in a section component. Visibility is the camelCase
 * `visibility` keys below, each tested `!== false` (undefined renders).
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING here is the skip link's "Skip to content"
 * (an a11y affordance, visible on focus only — PageBJ precedent).
 *
 * RENDER ORDER is the design's, which differs from the sister templates:
 * Header, Hero (#top), Marquee, Trust, Services, How (#how), Gallery, About,
 * Why, Testimonials (#reviews), Credentials, Area, Faq, Location (#visit),
 * then the closing band (#book, outside <main> as drawn) and the Footer with
 * its floating message pill.
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block below is prefixed
 * html[data-page="BW"] — the reset, body, img, a, ::selection and every
 * primitive — because index.astro bundles every wrapper's global CSS onto every
 * customer page.
 *
 * TOKEN PLAN (what an admin colour pick moves, and what it deliberately does
 * not). Mapped by ROLE onto the engine vocabulary:
 *   --paper #F1F0EB workshop grey ground · --paper-2 #E6E4DD the tinted bands
 *   (about, credentials, faq, the services band) · --card #DEDCD4 the photo and
 *   map plate · --ink #141414 text, every hairline, the small ink fills ·
 *   --ink-soft #55544F secondary copy · --accent #D9481A the safety-orange FILL
 *   (buttons, the closing band, the pin, the stars) · --accent-deep #B83A12
 *   orange TEXT on the light grounds (eyebrows, part numbers, hovers) ·
 *   --accent-light #FF8A5B orange text on the black bands.
 * FIXED, on purpose, under names the engine does not know:
 *   --shop #141414 / --on-shop #F1F0EB — the three black bands and the mobile
 *   drawer. They are the design's signature (a workshop's black paint), and
 *   keeping them fixed is what keeps every string on them legible under all six
 *   woodworks schemes: --accent-light on #141414 measures 5.6:1 (brown) or
 *   better, where the same eyebrow on a scheme-remapped ink band would sit at
 *   2.4:1 once "dark" or "black" turns ink white.
 *   --on-fill / --on-fill-alt — the label on an --accent fill and its inverse.
 *   Natively white / ink. Neither engine alias is right for all six schemes
 *   (--on-accent is picked against the scheme's LIGHT accent, --on-primary
 *   against its primary with a 0.5 luminance cut — both leave a white label on
 *   the gold, orange or black fill), so under an explicit scheme pick this file
 *   reads the scheme's --accent out of the override block and picks whichever
 *   of white / ink contrasts more (see __onFill below). Gated on the SCHEME,
 *   never on the override string alone: a font pick also makes that non-empty.
 *   --star — the review stars, a meaningful graphic (role="img") that needs
 *   3:1 on the ground. Natively the design's orange (#D9481A, 3.76:1). The
 *   engine's --accent is a FILL colour and falls to 2.26:1 ("gold") / 2.66:1
 *   ("orange") on its own paper, so under a scheme pick this file takes the
 *   first of the scheme's --accent / --accent-deep / --ink that reaches 3:1
 *   on its --paper (see __star below).
 * The map pin's keyline and the Leaflet zoom glyphs use --shop, not --ink: the
 * CARTO tiles never recolour, so they need the fixed ink under every scheme
 * (a remapped white ink vanishes into the light basemap).
 *
 * ACCESSIBILITY NOTE, stated not silently fixed: the design's white label on
 * its #D9481A fill measures 4.30:1 — under the 4.5:1 AA bar for 14-15px bold
 * caps, above the 3:1 bar for UI. It is the design's brand pairing, so it
 * ships; darkening --accent to #C03F16 clears AA and is a one-line change.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL: lib/astro-builder.ts defaults layout.fontPairing to
 * the literal 'modern', and resolveTheme's lockVariant does not blank it — so
 * without the two sentinel lines below buildOverrideCss would force Space
 * Grotesk + Inter over Archivo on nearly every real site.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES (lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts pins them): .btn-primary
 * .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right .testi .cta-band .trust,
 * and `hero` as a class. Buttons here are .btn--fill / .btn--line / .btn--ink /
 * .linkc; the header pill (.pill) and the floating pill (.fab) carry no .btn
 * at all.
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper defines window.__woodworksBWInitMap (family-unique) and
 * LocationBW calls that exact string. Keep `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot (it
 * erases the drawn fallback face) and keep id="map" literal. Tiles are the
 * design's CARTO light_all; lib/carto.ts appends the key at publish time.
 */
import HeaderBW from './header/HeaderBW.astro';
import HeroBW from './hero/HeroBW.astro';
import MarqueeBW from './marquee/MarqueeBW.astro';
import TrustBW from './trust/TrustBW.astro';
import ServicesBW from './services/ServicesBW.astro';
import HowBW from './how/HowBW.astro';
import GalleryBW from './gallery/GalleryBW.astro';
import AboutBW from './about/AboutBW.astro';
import WhyBW from './why/WhyBW.astro';
import TestimonialsBW from './testimonials/TestimonialsBW.astro';
import CredentialsBW from './credentials/CredentialsBW.astro';
import AreaBW from './area/AreaBW.astro';
import FaqBW from './faq/FaqBW.astro';
import LocationBW from './location/LocationBW.astro';
import CtaBandBW from './ctaBand/CtaBandBW.astro';
import FooterBW from './footer/FooterBW.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice (lib/astro-builder.ts).
// Treating it as unset keeps Archivo; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);

// Per-scheme fixes (see TOKEN PLAN above) read the scheme's own values out of
// the override block the engine just built, so they can never drift from the
// palette table. __tok returns one token's hex; the boundary keeps --paper from
// matching inside --on-paper, and --ink inside --on-ink.
const __tok = (name: string): string =>
  new RegExp('(?:^|[\\s;{])' + name + ':\\s*(#[0-9a-fA-F]{6})').exec(__overrideCss)?.[1] ?? '';
// The label on an --accent fill, recomputed for an explicit scheme pick.
const __hex = __tok('--accent');
const __lum = (hex: string): number => {
  const v = hex.replace('#', '');
  const ch = [0, 2, 4].map((k) => parseInt(v.slice(k, k + 2), 16) / 255)
    .map((s) => (s <= 0.03928 ? s / 12.92 : ((s + 0.055) / 1.055) ** 2.4));
  return 0.2126 * ch[0] + 0.7152 * ch[1] + 0.0722 * ch[2];
};
const __ratio = (a: string, b: string): number => {
  const x = __lum(a); const y = __lum(b);
  return (Math.max(x, y) + 0.05) / (Math.min(x, y) + 0.05);
};
const __onFill = __themeScheme && __hex
  ? (__ratio(__hex, '#FFFFFF') >= __ratio(__hex, '#141414') ? '#FFFFFF' : '#141414')
  : '';
// The review stars under a scheme pick (see TOKEN PLAN): the first of the
// scheme's fill / deep / ink colours that keeps 3:1 on its paper.
const __paperHex = __tok('--paper');
const __star = __themeScheme && __paperHex
  ? ([__hex, __tok('--accent-deep'), __tok('--ink')].find((c) => c && __ratio(c, __paperHex) >= 3) ?? '')
  : '';
// An admin FONT pick swaps Archivo's 72%-width display cut for a normal-width
// face, and the three giant sizes (hero h1, closing headline, footer wordmark)
// were drawn for the condensed one — a long word would then break mid-word on
// a phone. --disp-k scales those three by one constant (so no size can grow as
// the viewport narrows) and --glyph widens the wordmark's per-letter estimate.
// Gated on the pairing actually loading a font, never on the override string.
const __fontFix = __fontHref ? '--disp-k:.76;--glyph:.8;' : '';
// :root doubles the specificity so this wins over the static token block
// wherever Astro chooses to hoist that block.
const __schemeFix = (__onFill
  ? `--on-fill:${__onFill};--on-fill-alt:${__onFill === '#FFFFFF' ? '#141414' : '#FFFFFF'};`
  : '') + (__star ? `--star:${__star};` : '');
const __schemeFixCss = (__schemeFix || __fontFix)
  ? `html[data-page="BW"]:root{${__schemeFix}${__fontFix}}`
  : '';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BW">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A <meta> cannot read a CSS var, so this duplicates
       the workshop-grey ground token (--paper) the sticky header sits on. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#F1F0EB" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- The design's own families, verbatim from its <helmet>: Archivo with the
       WIDTH axis (62-125) as well as weight, because every headline is set by
       font-stretch, plus JetBrains Mono for the labels. -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wdth,wght@62..125,400..900&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {(layout.ogImage || layout.favicon) && <meta property="og:image" content={layout.ogImage || layout.favicon} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBW · "Molave" — woodworks. Tokens + shared base primitives. EVERY
       selector is prefixed html[data-page="BW"].

       1. SPECIFICITY. Appearance-bearing primitives are wrapped in :where(),
          so an Astro-scoped section rule (0,2,0) always wins over them.
       2. BUTTONS. .btn + .btn--fill / .btn--line / .btn--ink, each declaring
          its own background, border and label, and each :hover restating fill
          AND label so a label can never strand. Hovers are instant, as drawn.
       3. FOCUS. One DUO ring: a 3px paper outline inside a 6px ink halo — the
          ink halo shows on the grey ground, the paper outline on the black
          bands and on the orange one.
       4. HEAD ORDER. This block is followed by the scheme fix, the admin font
          link and, LAST in the head, the engine's override block.
          (Never write a literal closing style or script tag in here.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BW"] {
      /* grounds */
      --paper: #F1F0EB;
      --paper-2: #E6E4DD;
      --card: #DEDCD4;
      /* ink */
      --ink: #141414;
      --ink-soft: #55544F;
      --muted: #55544F;
      --line: #C5C4C0;
      /* safety orange: fill / text on light / text on black */
      --accent: #D9481A;
      --accent-deep: #B83A12;
      --accent-light: #FF8A5B;
      --accent-soft: #FF8A5B;
      /* rgb triplets for token-driven tints */
      --paper-rgb: 241,240,235;
      --ink-rgb: 20,20,20;
      --accent-rgb: 217,72,26;
      /* the engine's contrast aliases (declared for anything that reads them) */
      --on-primary: #FFFFFF;
      --on-accent: #FFFFFF;
      --on-ink: #F1F0EB;
      --on-paper: #141414;
      /* FIXED on purpose — names the engine does not know (see the frontmatter) */
      --shop: #141414;
      --on-shop: #F1F0EB;
      --on-shop-rgb: 241,240,235;
      --on-fill: #FFFFFF;
      --on-fill-alt: #141414;
      /* review stars — natively the orange; re-picked per scheme (__star) */
      --star: #D9481A;
      /* display-size factor + wordmark glyph estimate (see __fontFix) */
      --disp-k: 1;
      --glyph: .62;
      /* type + metrics */
      --disp: "Archivo", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --sans: "Archivo", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --serif: "Archivo", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --mono: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      --maxw: 1320px;
      --gutter: clamp(18px,4vw,48px);
    }

    /* VERIFIED CONTRAST (sRGB relative luminance, the design's palette):
       ink/paper 16.9 · ink/paper-2 15.2 · ink-soft/paper 7.0 · /paper-2 6.3
       accent-deep/paper 5.05 · /paper-2 4.5 · accent-light/shop 7.9
       on-shop/shop 16.9 · white/accent 4.30 (see the ACCESSIBILITY NOTE). */

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BW"] *,
    html[data-page="BW"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BW"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BW"] {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      /* The sticky header is 69px; every in-page target lands 12px under it. */
      scroll-padding-top: 81px;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BW"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BW"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.6;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    /* Element resets sit in :where() too: a bare `html[data-page] a` is (0,1,2)
       and would out-rank every (0,1,1) button primitive's label colour. */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(img) { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    /* The anchor pass at the end of <body> drops dead wayfinding links with the
       `hidden` attribute; every section styles its links with a display value,
       which would otherwise out-rank the UA's [hidden] rule. */
    html[data-page="BW"] [hidden] { display: none !important; }
    html[data-page="BW"] ::selection { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-fill); }
    /* text-transform is DECLARED, not defaulted: an unscoped uppercase rule in
       another wrapper once capitalised every template's headings. */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 800; color: inherit;
      letter-spacing: 0; line-height: inherit; text-transform: none;
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(p, dl, dd, ol, ul, figure, blockquote) { margin: 0; }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(ol, ul) { padding: 0; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.wrap) {
      max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--gutter);
    }

    /* ── .eyebrow — the numbered mono label over each section heading ── */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.eyebrow) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.6; letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none;
      color: var(--accent-deep); overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    /* ── .h2 — the condensed display heading. Two sizes, as drawn:
          .h2 (services / process / projects) and .h2--md (the rest). */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.h2) {
      margin: 12px 0 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 900;
      font-stretch: 75%; font-size: clamp(38px,5.6vw,80px); line-height: .92;
      letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: uppercase; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.h2--md) { font-size: clamp(34px,4.8vw,66px); line-height: .94; }
    /* With no eyebrow above it the heading opens the block. */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.h2:first-child) { margin-top: 0; }

    /* ── BUTTONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       .btn--fill  orange fill, white label   → hover: ink fill, paper label
       .btn--line  ink outline, ink label     → hover: ink fill, paper label
       .btn--ink   ink fill, paper label      → hover: orange fill, white label */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .5em;
      min-height: 54px; padding: 0 26px;
      border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 0;
      background-color: transparent; color: inherit;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2;
      letter-spacing: .02em; text-transform: uppercase; text-align: center;
      text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; cursor: pointer;
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn--fill) {
      background-color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-fill);
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn--line) {
      background-color: transparent; border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--ink);
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn--ink) {
      background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.btn--ink:hover) {
      background-color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-fill);
    }

    /* ── .linkc — the underlined text action (Directions). Carries no .btn. */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.linkc:hover) { color: var(--accent-deep); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

    /* ── FOCUS · the DUO ring ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(a, button, summary, [tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--ink);
    }

    /* ── skip link ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      padding: 12px 18px;
      font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
    }
    html[data-page="BW"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }
  </style>
  {__schemeFixCss && <style is:global set:html={__schemeFixCss}></style>}
  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBW layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.marqueeBlock !== false && <MarqueeBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBW content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBW layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline>
    // ANCHOR PASS. Each section component already resolves its in-page hrefs
    // against the ids this design CAN render (onPage), but a section that is
    // switched off, or has nothing to show, is not in the document — so a nav
    // entry or a button aimed at it would scroll nowhere.
    //
    // THE href ATTRIBUTE IS NEVER REWRITTEN. It is the owner's stored value:
    // the editor's link popover reads it straight off the element and saves it
    // back on every edit, so a rewritten href would silently become content
    // ('#services' stored as '#book' after one relabel).
    //  1. Wayfinding — a list marked data-anchor-list, or a secondary action
    //     marked data-anchor-drop ("See services" with no services on the page)
    //     — HIDES a dead entry: its label names a place that is not there.
    //  2. Every other dead in-page action keeps its href and is resolved when
    //     it is CLICKED: to the closing band, then the shop section, then the
    //     page top — never the section the action itself sits in. Inside the
    //     editor the bridge's capture-phase handler claims every hooked link
    //     first (preventDefault + stopPropagation), so this never runs there.
    // '#top' always resolves: HTML scrolls it to the top of the page.
    (function () {
      var idOf = function (a) {
        var h = a.getAttribute('href') || '';
        if (h.charAt(0) !== '#' || h.length < 2) return '';
        try { return decodeURIComponent(h.slice(1)); } catch (e) { return h.slice(1); }
      };
      var live = function (id) { return !id || id.toLowerCase() === 'top' || !!document.getElementById(id); };
      document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(function (a) {
        if (live(idOf(a))) return;
        if (a.closest('[data-anchor-list]')) { a.hidden = true; return; }
        if (a.hasAttribute('data-anchor-drop')) {
          a.hidden = true;
          // An action row left with nothing visible goes with it.
          var row = a.parentElement;
          if (row && !row.querySelector('a:not([hidden])')) row.setAttribute('data-empty', '');
        }
      });
      // A wayfinding list with every entry dropped leaves nothing to show…
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-anchor-list]').forEach(function (list) {
        if (!list.querySelector('a:not([hidden])')) list.setAttribute('data-empty', '');
      });
      // …and a container (marked data-collapse) whose every child is now empty
      // goes with it — innermost first, so the footer grid collapses before the
      // footer asks whether anything is left inside it.
      Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-collapse]')).reverse().forEach(function (box) {
        var kids = Array.prototype.slice.call(box.children);
        if (kids.every(function (k) { return k.hasAttribute('data-empty'); })) box.setAttribute('data-empty', '');
      });
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        if (e.defaultPrevented || e.button !== 0 || e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey) return;
        var a = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('a[href^="#"]') : null;
        if (!a || live(idOf(a))) return;
        var own = a.closest('section[id]');
        var to = ['book', 'visit', 'main'].filter(function (t) {
          return !!document.getElementById(t) && !(own && own.id === t);
        })[0];
        if (!to) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        // A real fragment navigation (scroll-padding, smooth scroll and the
        // focus starting point all follow it); the same hash twice would not
        // scroll again, so that case scrolls directly. Through a local name:
        // scripts/gen-template-fields.mjs reads any location-dot-word token in
        // a template as the location section's editable hook.
        var here = window.location;
        if (here.hash === '#' + to) document.getElementById(to).scrollIntoView();
        else here.hash = to;
      });
    })();
  </script>
  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      // Molave / BW Leaflet boot — accepts (lat, lng, label) from LocationBW.
      // The global name is family-unique on purpose: a preview harness can
      // render two wrappers in one document, and a shared name cross-wires maps.
      window.__woodworksBWInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
        if (!window.L) return;
        var el = document.getElementById('map'); if (!el) return;
        // Erases LocationBW's drawn fallback face; without this the tiles stack
        // on top of the drawn grid.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = L.map('map', { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 16);
        // The design's own CARTO style (light_all); lib/carto.ts appends the key
        // to this form at publish time. The design's grey is LocationBW's filter.
        L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/light_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { subdomains: 'abcd', maxZoom: 19, attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO' }).addTo(map);
        // The design's pin: an 18px orange square under a 2px ink keyline.
        // The fill is READ from the live --accent, so an explicit admin colour
        // pick recolours it. The keyline is the FIXED --shop ink, never the
        // scheme's --ink: the CARTO tiles stay light grey under every scheme,
        // and "dark"/"black" remap --ink (and "black" --accent) to white. A
        // fill too light to stand on those tiles (luminance > .5) takes the
        // keyline's ink instead, so the pin can never vanish.
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var shop = (cs.getPropertyValue('--shop') || '').trim() || '#141414';
        var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#D9481A';
        var lum = function (c) {
          var m = /^#([0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(c); if (!m) return 0;
          var v = parseInt(m[1], 16), w = [0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722], t = 0;
          [v >> 16 & 255, v >> 8 & 255, v & 255].forEach(function (x, k) {
            x /= 255; t += w[k] * (x <= 0.03928 ? x / 12.92 : Math.pow((x + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4));
          });
          return t;
        };
        var fill = lum(accent) > 0.5 ? shop : accent;
        var icon = L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:18px;height:18px;background:' + fill + ';border:2px solid ' + shop + ';"></div>',
          iconSize: [18, 18], iconAnchor: [9, 9]
        });
        // No popup and no tooltip — the design draws neither. The map frame's
        // aria-label already names the place; the pin itself is not a control.
        L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon, keyboard: false, interactive: false }).addTo(map);
      };
    })();
  </script>
